<title>USA: Inter-Continental Hotels plans hotels in Brazil.</title>
<headline>Inter-Continental Hotels plans hotels in Brazil.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Inter-Continental Hotels and Resorts said Monday its Americas division had a joint venture agreement with Brazilian developer Brascan Imobilaria S.A. to build and manage 12 Inter-Continental or Forum brand hotels in Brazil by 2000.</p>
<p>Inter-Continental is a unit of privately-held Saison Group, an investor group based in Japan.</p>
<p>The two companies first formed a joint venture to build the Hotel Inter-Continental Rio and the newly-opened Hotel Inter-Continental Sao Paolo.</p>
<p>Inter-Continental, which owns over 195 hotels in 69 countries, said it was trying to increase its Forum brand and its Resort portfolio in Latin America.</p>
</text>
